# .brewpageignore -- publish-scope filter for the RAG Guide static bundle.
#
# Purpose: the repo folder carries manuscript + scaffold + dev tooling (~137 files),
# which blows past the BrewPage site caps (< 100 files / < 20 MB total / < 5 MB per file).
# This file lists DEV-ONLY paths to exclude so only the live static site is published.
# It is repo-keeping vs publish-scope: excluded files STAY in git, they just do not ship.
#
# Syntax: gitignore-style globs. A leading-and-trailing slash-free name matches at any
# depth. The CI bundler (direct REST today; brewpage-action / brewpage CLI later) applies
# this file against recipes/rag-guide/ to produce the upload manifest.
#
# DO NOT exclude anything the live site fetches/imports at runtime. Audited 2026-06-14:
#   - all 12 *.html pages, shared/css/**, shared/js/**, shared/data/** (JSON + JS the
#     pages import or fetch), shared/og/*.png|ico|svg, sitemap.xml  -> KEPT.
#   - shared/components/*.html are authoring-time copy-in partials (the markup is inlined
#     into each page; nothing fetches them at runtime) -> EXCLUDED (see runbook).
#
# Verified final published set: 84 files / 1.69 MB / largest 0.16 MB. All caps satisfied.

# --- AI/agent + tooling state (every depth) ---
.claude/
*.log

# --- Manuscript source (md-as-source, hand-ported to HTML; not shipped) ---
content/

# --- Design exploration / mockups ---
mokups/

# --- All Markdown (design docs, AtlasMD, READMEs) at every depth ---
*.md

# --- Build scripts / generators (no build step ships) ---
*.py
scripts/

# --- Authoring-time HTML partials: inlined into pages, never fetched at runtime ---
shared/components/

# --- Editor + OS junk and backups ---
*.bak
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.gitkeep

# --- Design-source SVG whose rasterized counterpart is what the site references.
#     og-rag-guide.png is the referenced OG image; the SVG is source only.
#     NOTE: favicon.svg IS referenced by the pages -> intentionally NOT excluded here.
shared/og/og-rag-guide.svg
